  "text": "If you're looking for a simple Neapolitan ice cream recipe, here are some basic steps to follow:\n\n1. Start by selecting high-quality chocolate. This is important because Neapolitan ice cream is known for its rich chocolate flavor.\n2. Take a small amount of chocolate and melt it down in a pan, ideally a pan that's not too hot. This process should be done carefully to prevent the chocolate from burning.\n3. Once the chocolate has melted, take it off the heat and let it cool down for a few minutes.\n4. In a separate bowl, place some milk and mix it with the melted chocolate. Ensure that the mixture is evenly distributed.\n5. Now, take the mixture and pour it into a container. Cover the container and place it in the refrigerator for a few hours.\n6. After the mixture has been in the refrigerator long enough, take it out and allow it to reach a temperature that's just below the boiling point.\n7. Once the mixture is ready, take it and pour it into an ice cream maker.\n\nAlthough chocolate is a crucial component of Neapolitan ice cream, it's important to keep in mind that you might want to use a smaller amount of chocolate during this process. If you're unsure about how to use the right amount of chocolate, you might want to start by using half the amount you're used to. This will help ensure that the chocolate flavor doesn't overpower the rest of the recipe.",
